{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B2wUFvhEzLfsM9RX5WYjC6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Backlog: widget foundation: support several widget kinds\n2\t\n3\tcreated: 2026-10-29\n4\t\n5\t## What\n6\t\n7\tMake the native widget foundation serve more than one widget. Today it only\n8\tknows Your Day: one cached payload, a hardcoded `your-day` fetch path, and\n9\t`YourDayPayload` / `YourDayWidgetProvider` referenced from the fetch worker,\n10\tthe action receiver and worker, `WidgetWork`, `WidgetCache` and\n11\t`WidgetBridgePlugin`. After this job, adding a widget means: a kind entry, a\n12\tprovider with its layout, and an API endpoint.\n13\t\n14\t**No visible change:** Your Day must look and behave exactly as before. The\n15\ttime tracking widget ([[android-widget-time-tracking]]) is the first to use\n16\tthis.\n17\t\n18\t## Why\n19\t\n20\tThe decisions (`docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets-decisions.md`, D2/D8)\n21\tpromise that a new widget is \"mostly a backend endpoint plus a native\n22\tlayout\". The current code does not deliver that yet.\n23\t\n24\t## Steps\n25\t\n26\t1. **A kind registry:** one place listing each widget kind with its `kind`\n27\t   string (as in the payload), its API path (`/api/v1/widgets/<kind>`) and its\n28\t   provider class. For now only `your-day`.\n29\t2. **Generic payload:** rename `YourDayPayload` to a generic name (for\n30\t   example `WidgetPayload`); the format is shared by all widgets. The parser\n31\t   keeps today's behaviour (unknown fields, section keys, icons and action\n32\t   types are ignored).\n33\t3. **Cache per kind** (`WidgetCache`): payload, fetch time, the outdated flag\n34\t   and action state are stored per kind. The overall state (signed out,\n35\t   server without widgets, update the app, device not supported) stays global:\n36\t   it is about the token and the server, not a widget. Keep everything in the\n37\t   one existing `widget_cache` prefs file with kind-prefixed keys, so the\n38\t   backup exclusion rules need no change. On first start after the update,\n39\t   drop the old unprefixed payload keys and fetch again; no migration of the\n40\t   old cache.\n41\t4. **Fetching:** the fetch worker fetches every kind that has at least one\n42\t   placed widget, each from its own path. 401, 404 on a widget route and 426\n43\t   change the global state as today; a 429/5xx/offline marks only that kind\n44\t   as outdated. `refresh_at` is optional per kind (time tracking has none).\n45\t5. **Scheduling:** the periodic work runs while any widget of any kind is\n46\t   placed, and is cancelled when the last one is removed (instead of Your\n47\t   Day's `onEnabled`/`onDisabled` alone). `fetchNow` runs when any kind is\n48\t   placed.\n49\t6. **Actions:** the action fill-in intent carries the kind. The receiver and\n50\t   worker look up the row in that kind's cache, keep action state per kind,\n51\t   and after an action re-fetch **all** placed kinds (a change can show on\n52\t   more than one widget).\n53\t7. **Updating views:** one `updateAll` that re-renders every kind's\n54\t   providers; `WidgetBridgePlugin` (`clear`, `unsupported`, `setToken`) and the\n55\t   workers use it.\n56\t8. **Manual checks:** Your Day as before (data, tap a todo row, tap-to-\n57\t   complete, offline, logout, unsupported server); update from the previous\n58\t   build with a Your Day widget placed (it refreshes and keeps working).\n59\t\n60\t## Out of scope\n61\t\n62\t- The time tracking widget and the format additions it needs\n63\t  ([[android-widget-time-tracking]]).\n64\t- Any change to Your Day's look or behaviour.\n65\t\n66\t## Notes\n67\t\n68\t- Keep `WidgetTokenStore` as it is: one token serves all widgets.\n69\t- Do not add new dependencies.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d08818e-a718-4681-9dcb-edc4bb179adb","uuid":"b3b9549e-40c2-4d81-a96e-b73bc65c0ccf","timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:50:26.923Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/backlog/android-widget-foundation-multiple-kinds.md","content":"# Backlog: widget foundation: support several widget kinds\n\ncreated: 2026-10-29\n\n## What\n\nMake the native widget foundation serve more than one widget. Today it only\nknows Your Day: one cached payload, a hardcoded `your-day` fetch path, and\n`YourDayPayload` / `YourDayWidgetProvider` referenced from the fetch worker,\nthe action receiver and worker, `WidgetWork`, `WidgetCache` and\n`WidgetBridgePlugin`. After this job, adding a widget means: a kind entry, a\nprovider with its layout, and an API endpoint.\n\n**No visible change:** Your Day must look and behave exactly as before. The\ntime tracking widget ([[android-widget-time-tracking]]) is the first to use\nthis.\n\n## Why\n\nThe decisions (`docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets-decisions.md`, D2/D8)\npromise that a new widget is \"mostly a backend endpoint plus a native\nlayout\". The current code does not deliver that yet.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **A kind registry:** one place listing each widget kind with its `kind`\n   string (as in the payload), its API path (`/api/v1/widgets/<kind>`) and its\n   provider class. For now only `your-day`.\n2. **Generic payload:** rename `YourDayPayload` to a generic name (for\n   example `WidgetPayload`); the format is shared by all widgets. The parser\n   keeps today's behaviour (unknown fields, section keys, icons and action\n   types are ignored).\n3. **Cache per kind** (`WidgetCache`): payload, fetch time, the outdated flag\n   and action state are stored per kind. The overall state (signed out,\n   server without widgets, update the app, device not supported) stays global:\n   it is about the token and the server, not a widget. Keep everything in the\n   one existing `widget_cache` prefs file with kind-prefixed keys, so the\n   backup exclusion rules need no change. On first start after the update,\n   drop the old unprefixed payload keys and fetch again; no migration of the\n   old cache.\n4. **Fetching:** the fetch worker fetches every kind that has at least one\n   placed widget, each from its own path. 401, 404 on a widget route and 426\n   change the global state as today; a 429/5xx/offline marks only that kind\n   as outdated. `refresh_at` is optional per kind (time tracking has none).\n5. **Scheduling:** the periodic work runs while any widget of any kind is\n   placed, and is cancelled when the last one is removed (instead of Your\n   Day's `onEnabled`/`onDisabled` alone). `fetchNow` runs when any kind is\n   placed.\n6. **Actions:** the action fill-in intent carries the kind. The receiver and\n   worker look up the row in that kind's cache, keep action state per kind,\n   and after an action re-fetch **all** placed kinds (a change can show on\n   more than one widget).\n7. **Updating views:** one `updateAll` that re-renders every kind's\n   providers; `WidgetBridgePlugin` (`clear`, `unsupported`, `setToken`) and the\n   workers use it.\n8. **Manual checks:** Your Day as before (data, tap a todo row, tap-to-\n   complete, offline, logout, unsupported server); update from the previous\n   build with a Your Day widget placed (it refreshes and keeps working).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- The time tracking widget and the format additions it needs\n  ([[android-widget-time-tracking]]).\n- Any change to Your Day's look or behaviour.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Keep `WidgetTokenStore` as it is: one token serves all widgets.\n- Do not add new dependencies.\n","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":70}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01B2wUFvhEzLfsM9RX5WYjC6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
