, widget/YourDayWidgetProvider.java, widget/WidgetFetchWorker.java, widget/WidgetActionReceiver.java, widget/WidgetActionWorker.java (call sites pass the kind)","+  depends: TASK-1","+  risk: medium — upgrade path: after the old keys are dropped the global state can still be `OK` while Your Day has no payload, and today's render shows \"update the app\" for that case (`payload == null` under `OK`); render must show the loading text instead until the re-fetch lands (see TASK-8), or the upgrade causes a visible glitch.","+","+TASK-5: Add one central `updateAll(context)` (e.g. on `WidgetKind`/a small static helper next to it) that re-renders every registered kind's provider, plus an \"any widget of any kind placed\" check, and switch `WidgetBridgePlugin` (`load`, `clear`, `unsupported`, `setToken`) and both workers to them.","+  files: widget/WidgetKind.java, widget/YourDayWidgetProvider.java (keeps its own per-provider render and `hasWidgets`), WidgetBridgePlugin.java, widget/WidgetFetchWorker.java, widget/WidgetActionWorker.java, widget/WidgetActionReceiver.java","+  depends: TASK-1","+  risk: low — call-site swap; `YourDayWidgetProvider.updateAll` remains the per-kind render the registry points to.","+","+TASK-6: Make the fetch worker loop over every kind with at least one placed widget, fetching each from its own path: 401 clears token+cache and stops the loop, 404 sets `UNSUPPORTED_SERVER` and 426 (or a newer `schema_version`) sets `UPDATE_APP` globally as today, 429/5xx/offline/unparseable marks only that kind outdated, a success saves that kind; retry when any kind failed temporarily; schedule the `refresh_at` fetch only for kinds that send one, using a per-kind unique work name (e.g. `widget-fetch-at-refresh-<kind>`).","+  files: widget/WidgetFetchWorker.java, widget/WidgetWork.java (`fetchAt` takes the kind; `cancelAll` cancels every kind's refresh work)","+  depends: TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5","+  risk: medium — the order of global vs per-kind outcomes in one run (e.g. one kind OK, the next 401) and the \"token changed during the request\" check must still hold per request; with one kind it must behave exactly like today.","+","+TASK-7: Tie scheduling to \"any kind placed\": `WidgetWork.fetchNow` runs when any registered kind has widgets, the fetch worker's early exit uses the same check, and `YourDayWidgetProvider.onDisabled` only cancels all work when no widget of any kind is left (`onEnabled`/`onUpdate` keep scheduling the periodic work).","+  files: widget/WidgetWork.java, widget/YourDayWidgetProvider.java, widget/WidgetFetchWorker.java","+  depends: TASK-5","+  risk: medium — getting the \"last widget removed\" check wrong either leaves background work running with no widget (D9) or cancels it while another kind is still placed.","+","+TASK-8: Pass the kind through the action path: the provider adds an `EXTRA_ACTION_KIND` to the checkbox fill-in intent; the receiver validates it against the registry, looks the row up in that kind's cached payload and starts the action in that kind's action state; `WidgetWork.runAction` puts the kind into the input data and the unique work name (e.g. `widget-action-<kind>-<id>`); the worker finishes/reverts in that kind's state and, after success or 404, re-fetches all placed kinds via `fetchNow`. Also update the provider's render to read its own kind's cache and show the loading text when the global state is `OK` but its kind has no payload yet.","+  files: widget/YourDayWidgetProvider.java, widget/WidgetActionReceiver.java, widget/WidgetActionWorker.java, widget/WidgetWork.java","+  depends: TASK-2, TASK-4, TASK-5","+  risk: medium — the fill-in extras are untrusted (D3): an unknown or missing kind must be rejected and re-render to undo the launcher's local CheckBox toggle, exactly like an invalid key today; an action enqueued by the old build (no kind in its input data) must be treated as `your-day` or dropped safely — the developer should pick one and note it.","+","+TASK-9: Run the manual checks from the brief on a device/emulator and record the results in implementation.md: Your Day shows data, row tap opens the todo, tap-to-complete, offline (outdated label), logout (signed-out text), unsupported server, and an in-place update from the previous build with a Your Day widget placed (it refreshes and keeps working, no \"update the app\" flash).","+  files: docs/jobs/eat_widget-foundation-support-several-widget-kinds/implementation.md","+  depends: TASK-1 … TASK-8","+  risk: medium — needs a device and a reachable widget-capable API; if the developer cannot run them, they must say so in implementation.md rather than mark them done.","+","+## Notes for the developer","+","+- `WidgetTokenStore`, the manifest, `backup_rules.xml`, `data_extraction_rules.xml`, layouts and strings should not change; if one of them seems to need a change, flag it.","+- The brief leaves open whether a newer `schema_version` from one kind should be global; this plan keeps today's behaviour (global `UPDATE_APP`), since the time tracking job keeps `schema_version` at 1.","+- No new base provider class: shared provider behaviour (schedule on enable, cancel on last disable) goes through static helpers in `WidgetWork`, matching the existing style."]}],"originalFile":"# Tasks: widget foundation: support several widget kinds\n\nid: eat\nanalyst:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n<!-- TASK-1: description\n     files: list of files likely affected\n     depends: none\n     risk: low / medium / high — reason\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011vSVVB2xjnLSSS6A77izrP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
