{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgX7NTfroo9UiJYEvQPfY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the task list to `docs/jobs/eat_widget-foundation-support-several-widget-kinds/tasks.md`. I couldn't check that I'm on the job branch, because this session has no shell to run `git branch --show-current`.\n\nThe work is 9 tasks, all in `android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/`:\n\n1. **Kind registry:** a new `WidgetKind` file listing each kind with its kind string, API path, provider, how to redraw that provider, and its section keys. For now only `your-day`.\n2. **Generic payload:** rename `YourDayPayload` to `WidgetPayload`, and `parse` checks the kind it expects. Your Day parsing stays exactly the same.\n3. **Fetch path:** `WidgetApi` fetches each kind from its own path instead of the hardcoded `your-day` one.\n4. **Cache per kind:** `WidgetCache` stores each kind's data under prefixed keys in the same `widget_cache` file. The signed-out / server / update / device state stays global. The old keys are dropped once after the update, with no migration.\n5. **One `updateAll`:** a single call that redraws every kind's widgets, plus an \"any widget placed\" check. `WidgetBridgePlugin` and both workers use them.\n6. **Fetch worker:** loops over every placed kind. 401, 404 and 426 change the global state as today; 429, 5xx and offline mark only that kind as outdated. `refresh_at` is optional per kind.\n7. **Scheduling:** background work runs while any widget is placed, and Your Day's `onDisabled` only cancels it when no widget of any kind is left.\n8. **Actions:** the tap intent carries the kind, which is checked against the registry. Action state is kept per kind, and after an action all placed kinds are fetched again.\n9. **Manual checks** from the brief, including updating from the previous build with a Your Day widget placed.\n\nThings the developer needs to watch:\n- **Visible glitch after the update:** once the old cache is dropped, the global state can still be \"OK\" while Your Day has no data. Today that shows \"Please update the app\". TASK-8 changes it to show the loading text until the new fetch arrives.\n- **Leftover actions from the old build:** an action queued before the update has no kind attached. The developer should either treat it as `your-day` or drop it safely, and note which.\n- **One decision I made:** the brief doesn't say whether a newer `schema_version` from one kind is global. The plan keeps today's behaviour (a global \"update the app\").\n\nThere are no Android unit tests in the repo, so the checks are a compile (`./gradlew assembleDebug`, if the Android SDK is available) and the manual run on a device."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4851,"cache_read_input_tokens":56865,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4851},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d08818e-a718-4681-9dcb-edc4bb179adb","uuid":"8c56b6ec-7459-42a3-98d1-11e28fccca26","timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:51:23.063Z","request_id":"req_011CgX7NTJXg4KWRgNyP1yLU"}
